# Committed production build defaults (loaded by `vite build`, i.e. every
# `make installer-*`). These pin the shipped binary at the prod cloud API, the
# local sidecar, and the hosted prod coordinator as the default a fresh install
# connects to. A user can still point at their own household / cooperative
# coordinator at runtime via Settings. An explicit override outranks this
# default, and the mesh daemon's reported coordinator is adopted when there is
# no explicit override. Shipping localhost as the default would leave fresh
# installs pointed at nothing until the daemon reports in.
#
# Warning: `.env.local` also loads in production builds and outranks this file.
# Personal machine overrides (e.g. a Tailscale coordinator IP) therefore belong
# in `.env.development.local` (dev-mode only), never `.env.local`, or they leak
# into release installers. See `.env.example`.

VITE_CLOUD_API_URL=https://api.trypotluck.ai
VITE_LOCAL_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8321
VITE_COORDINATOR_URL=https://coordinator.trypotluck.ai
